<h2 id="intersection-section-conventions" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0AZ8">43.2</span> Conventions</h2>

<p>
We fix an algebraically closed ground field $\mathbf{C}$ of any characteristic. All schemes and varieties are over $\mathbf{C}$ and all morphisms are over $\mathbf{C}$. A variety $X$ is <em>nonsingular</em> if $X$ is a regular scheme (see Properties, Definition <a href="/tag/02IS" data-tag="02IS">28.9.1</a>). In our case this means that the morphism $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{C})$ is smooth (see Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/038X" data-tag="038X">33.12.6</a>). 
</p>
